  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Humanitarian Response for Vulnerable People on the Move in Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the International Organization for Migration (IOM) Humanitarian Response Plan for 2024 and 2025, the Organization is contributing to the improvement of migrants&#x2019; humanitarian conditions at the national and local levels in Mexico with special provisions for migrants in vulnerable situations. Over a ten-month period, IOM is implementing a multi-sectoral response to migrants across Mexico, including the operationalization of multi-purpose community centres, capacity building of local actors to facilitate migrant access to health care and mental health and psychosocial support; provision of food aid; distribution of equipment and non-food items, among others. Complementing humanitarian assistance, IOM implements innovative infrastructure projects, facilitates access to internet connectivity and continues with the provision of critical protection services and data collection exercises to inform the response, among other activities to enhance the self-sufficiency, sustainability and autonomy of migrant shelters.</narrative>
  </description>
